{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20363",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.65,
      "end_seconds": 4.66,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Sorry I'm a a little late, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.41,
      "end_seconds": 11.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 16.02,
      "end_seconds": 20.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Good morning, doctor. I came along to help out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.58,
      "end_seconds": 31.03,
      "duration_seconds": 9.45,
      "text": "I mean, honestly, it's some chest discomfort when I climb stairs, and my family pushed me to come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.99,
      "end_seconds": 40.58,
      "duration_seconds": 8.59,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 44.38,
      "end_seconds": 54.94,
      "duration_seconds": 10.56,
      "text": "I'd call it severe yes, stairs that makes it worse i've had indigestion after tablets too, for about three months"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.75,
      "end_seconds": 59.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Is there something that settles it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.85,
      "end_seconds": 70.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.44,
      "text": "It, It settles a little with milk. I've, I've also had bruising easily."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.02,
      "end_seconds": 85.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Right, what operations have you had, if any?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.25,
      "end_seconds": 90.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Just a bunion operation, six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.88,
      "end_seconds": 94.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Okay, and alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.06,
      "end_seconds": 100.11,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 103.92,
      "end_seconds": 105.28,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Right, any smoking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.02,
      "end_seconds": 109.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.71,
      "text": "I gave up cigarettes last spring"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.16,
      "end_seconds": 114.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "What do you do during the day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.87,
      "end_seconds": 123.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.94,
      "text": "I look after my grandchildren most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.49,
      "end_seconds": 126.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "How are your meals?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.83,
      "end_seconds": 131.86,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 133.24,
      "end_seconds": 137.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "Any inherited conditions that you know of in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 138.06,
      "end_seconds": 140.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "My grandfather had a stroke."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.81,
      "end_seconds": 152.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 154.88,
      "end_seconds": 161.52,
      "duration_seconds": 6.64,
      "text": "I have heart disease, for about ten years. I've, I've got high cholesterol."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.62,
      "end_seconds": 171.7,
      "duration_seconds": 8.08,
      "text": "yes, heart disease is known to us, good to have that clear. What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.45,
      "end_seconds": 177.63,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Clopidogrel. I take it 75 milligrams, maybe, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.63,
      "end_seconds": 183.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Did you happen to bring the box or the paperwork?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.66,
      "end_seconds": 195.77,
      "duration_seconds": 11.11,
      "text": "Erm, no, it's at home. I take simvastatin, 20 milligrams, at night. My neighbour said I should get it looked at."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.34,
      "end_seconds": 201.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.89,
      "text": "Let me ask about allergies, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 205.29,
      "end_seconds": 207.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "I've never had an allergy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.68,
      "end_seconds": 211.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.86,
      "text": "Any breathlessness or pain at rest?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.18,
      "end_seconds": 214.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "no, nothing to report there"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.71,
      "end_seconds": 219.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "any black stools, fainting or palpitations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.7,
      "end_seconds": 225.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "No black stools, fainting or palpitations, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.25,
      "end_seconds": 228.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.25,
      "end_seconds": 232.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "No, um, that's all fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.19,
      "end_seconds": 236.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.61,
      "text": "Let's start with the basic checks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.96,
      "end_seconds": 246.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "sit still for a moment.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.59,
      "end_seconds": 273.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.95,
      "text": "okay: BP is 126 over 74, saturation 99 percent, pulse is 67 beats a minute, temperature 36.4, respiratory rate 16."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.87,
      "end_seconds": 280.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "alright, over here please and I'll take a look"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 292.66,
      "end_seconds": 293.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.25,
      "end_seconds": 296.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Look straight ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.61,
      "end_seconds": 312.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.03,
      "text": "Heart sounds are normal and your chest is clear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.08,
      "end_seconds": 315.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.27,
      "end_seconds": 319.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 335.07,
      "end_seconds": 339.05,
      "duration_seconds": 3.98,
      "text": "there are a few small bruises on your forearms"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 343.76,
      "end_seconds": 352.85,
      "duration_seconds": 9.09,
      "text": "Please sit back down. Having listened and examined, this looks most like stable coronary disease on antiplatelet treatment, with minor bleeding."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 354.39,
      "end_seconds": 357.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "What are the odds it's serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 358.56,
      "end_seconds": 388.73,
      "duration_seconds": 30.17,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now stable coronary disease on antiplatelet treatment, with minor bleeding is my leading thought, not anything worse. I think a lipid profile makes sense here, for cardiovascular risk. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I think an ECG makes sense here, for chest discomfort. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 389.85,
      "end_seconds": 406.23,
      "duration_seconds": 16.38,
      "text": "I'm going to put you on pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast, long term. You take it by mouth. That's for stomach protection. Take your blood-thinning tablets after food and do not stop them on your own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 406.64,
      "end_seconds": 420.61,
      "duration_seconds": 13.97,
      "text": "I follow. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 424.47,
      "end_seconds": 429.26,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "actually, um, okay, that makes sense thanks for explaining"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 430.27,
      "end_seconds": 431.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Goodbye for now."
    }
  ]
}